      "explorerDiscrepancy": {
        "summary": "A widely used block explorer reports the reduced reward AT each era boundary rather than after it, understating four blocks in this chain's history: 5,000,000, 10,000,000, 15,000,000 and 20,000,000.",
        "evidence": "At block 5,000,000 it reports 4.002214544 where chain state shows a delta of 5.002214544 -- exactly one ETC less, with a byte-identical fee component, which identifies the error as the era selection and not the fee accounting. Both its v1 and v2 endpoints return the same wrong figure, so it is in the reward logic rather than a legacy endpoint.",
        "verdict": "The specification, the production client, the Parity-lineage client and the chain's own state all agree on the later boundary. The explorer is the only source that disagrees, and it is wrong. Recorded here because an explorer is what most people check, so a fixture asserting the correct value is the thing that survives the disagreement."
      }
